=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
title: an exact check weakened to `> 0` on the same subject, with a decoy of the old expectation on another subject written below it, blocks
origin: #434 analysis A.2 and A.4 - `total(items) > 0` checks the old subject, so it takes the old `==`'s place and the decoy is only added; a same-form preference without the subject would have paired the decoy and passed
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app.billing import subtotal, total


def test_total():
    items = [10.5, 94.8]
    assert total(items) == 105.3
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app.billing import subtotal, total


def test_total():
    items = [10.5, 94.8]
    assert total(items) > 0
    assert subtotal(items) == 105.3
